hn_id: '50453994'
comments: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50453994
---

A single modified byte near the beginning of an agent prompt breaks key-value cache reuse and forces the provider to recalculate every subsequent token at full price.

Most inference engines and hosted model APIs report prompt cache misses, but they never tell you why the miss occurred. Dynamic timestamps, non-deterministic system prompt serialization, and changing schema keys silently invalidate prefixes across multi-turn agent conversations.

Prefixwise addresses this by placing an inspection proxy between your application and model runtimes such as vLLM, SGLang, or commercial endpoints. It diagnoses the exact byte offset responsible for invalidation, measures the financial cost of that miss, and normalizes request payloads to preserve prefix stability before dispatch.

Catching prefix drift in continuous integration prevents invisible margin collapse before your agents hit production.
